  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x)\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\sqrt{2}-1.$",
